From cfbcf62d42b2da01904df1cd0ffecf1c2b028b9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aadilparmar <124196983+aadilparmar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Apr 2026 12:21:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] perf: edge-cache public APIs, kill pageview tracker,
 rate-limit upload
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- /api/settings, /api/stats/live, 8 public GET routes now use
  Cache-Control: public, s-maxage=300, stale-while-revalidate=86400
  so Vercel's CDN serves cached responses to all visitors.
- Remove cache:'no-store' overrides in fetchConfig/fetchLiveStats so
  the client actually benefits from the new CDN caching.
- Drop <PageTracker/> from the root layout — GA already covers the
  same analytics and the /api/track/pageview call was firing on every
  navigation, burning function invocations at 75% of the monthly limit.
- /api/upload: 10 uploads per 10 min per IP via existing rate limiter.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
